# Force LF on checkout regardless of the platform/runner's core.autocrlf —
# without eol=lf, `text=auto` alone still lets Windows checkouts convert to
# CRLF, which breaks exact-text fixture assertions (found via real Windows
# CI: test/unit/javascript.test.ts "range without --expand" failed only on
# windows-latest, comparing `\n` fixtures against a CRLF-converted checkout).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Built grammar artifacts are binary; never run text normalization on them
*.wasm binary
